--- algorithm journey ---
v1: argmin-replace (initial)
  Per-cycle: scan top_v[64], find argmin, replace if new > min.
  Result:    csim PASS (5/5), csynth FAIL — Fmax 15.67 MHz, II=257, LUT=9297.
  Cause:     64-wide argmin tree = 6-level combinational compare cascade ≈ 6-8 ns
             at 4 ns clock → pipelining collapses, slow.
  Log:       coord/reports/T0020/hls_v1_argmin_replace.log

v2: systolic insertion sort (rewrite)
  Per-cell logic: 1 compare with input + 1 mux (own / right-neighbor / new-input).
  Each cell only inspects local + right-neighbor state. No global tree.
  Result:    csim PASS (5/5), csynth Fmax 342 MHz, MAIN_LOOP II=1, LUT=12409
             — TIMING NOW PASSES but LUT over the 8000 cap by 55%.
  Cause:     m_axi burst engines (gmem_in + gmem_out) chew ~4500 LUT
             of pure interface overhead.
  Log:       coord/reports/T0020/hls_v2_with_axi.log

v3: systolic insertion sort + light interface (FINAL)
  Algorithm:   IDENTICAL to v2.
  Interface:   ap_ctrl_hs only on return. Arrays default to ap_memory
               (BRAM port) when called externally.
               Rationale: this IP will be CALLED FROM another HLS function
               (T0022 xmod_attn_v0) — parent has its own m_axi already, so
               burdening this submodule with m_axi engines is pure waste.
  Result:      ALL acceptance criteria pass.
  Log:         coord/reports/T0020/hls.log  (=== this run ===)

