--- design notes for T0022 reuse ---
Call from parent HLS as:
    int16_t  top_scores[64];
    uint16_t top_indices[64];
    topk_engine(my_256_scores, top_scores, top_indices);

Output order: top_v is sorted ASCENDING (top_v[0] = K-th largest, i.e. the
threshold; top_v[K-1] = global max). top_i carries the corresponding input
indices. The SET of indices is what xmod_attn_v0 needs to gather V[selected].

When inlined into T0022, expect the LUT count to grow ~6700 + AXI of the
parent — well within the 80,000 LUT budget for T0022.

